<title>UK: Syria buys one cargo raw sugar for November -trade.</title>
<headline>Syria buys one cargo raw sugar for November -trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria bought 13,000 tonnes of raw sugar at $311.50 per tonne c &amp; f for shipment in November, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The price was to include bagging costs, they said. Details of the supplier have yet to emerge.</p>
<p>Earlier on Friday, market sources said Syria bought a cargo of white sugar at $368.95 per tonne, with the supplier believed to be a European trade house. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
